PARITY NOTES (native reproduces the web source's data, composition, states and i18n)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web ResultPanel is a pure, prop-driven presentational component (props: title, data?, error?,
  idleMessage?). It owns NO data source and has exactly three mutually-exclusive render branches in this
  precedence: error -> rose/danger text (red-tinted card); data != null -> JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)
  in a scrollable <pre> + CopyButton (green-tinted card); else -> italic muted `idleMessage ?? "No result
  yet"` (neutral card). The header always shows `title` (small, secondary) and the CopyButton iff data != null
  (even while an error is shown — reproduced as HasCopyAction).

  Native reproduction:
    - ResultPanelProjection (the cached->projection adapter) reproduces the branch precedence, the two-space
      indented serialization, the per-state semantic tint tokens (TsColorDanger/Success/TextPrimary brushes,
      never neon), and routes every owned string through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade.
    - ResultPanel.cs (WinUI ContentControl) binds Title/Data/Error/IdleMessage as bindable DPs (the web props),
      renders via the shared ResultPanelViewModel (no HTTP in the view), uses the shared TsCopyButton, JetBrains
      Mono (TsTypeFontFamilyMono) for the <pre>, design tokens for every colour/space/radius, names the card as
      an Automation region, announces the body as a live region per state, and emits view.opened on Loaded.
    - States: the generic loading / stale / offline branches are intentionally NOT present because the web
      source has none (it is presentational and prop-driven). This mirrors the established QuickNavWidget
      precedent ("There is deliberately no loading / error / stale / offline state because the web source has
      none"). The web's three real branches (error / result / idle-empty) are all reproduced and tested.
    - i18n: the web source itself is anonymous (no t() calls — title/error/idleMessage are caller-fed). The
      strings this surface owns route through the facade with English fallbacks (the sibling-widget convention;
      keys are not added to Strings/*/Resources.resw here): featureView.resultPanel.noResult = "No result yet",
      featureView.resultPanel.title = "Result", featureView.resultPanel.resultReady = "Result ready",
      common.copyButton.copy = "Copy", common.copyButton.copied = "Copied" (the last two match the web CopyButton).

